cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "NeoFOAM: a performance-portable finite-volume CFD framework"
abstract: >-
  NeoFOAM is an open-source performance-portable finite-volume CFD framework built on
  top of NeoN and primarily implemented in modern C++. It targets heterogeneous
  computing systems, so the same solver implementation runs on CPUs and GPUs from
  NVIDIA, AMD and Intel while staying portable across Linux, macOS and Windows.
  NeoFOAM provides fluid-flow solvers corresponding to established OpenFOAM solvers,
  OpenFOAM-compatible mesh and field conversion utilities, and a Python framework for
  composing and running cases.
type: software
